Optical power, spectra, images, and model-defined features (@met-optical: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metrology, #source "../sources/SI-Realizations.lingua#r_240WHEHDVW9TR241AXP6T4STM0", #source "../sources/Dimensional-Metrology.lingua#r_5XRAV7WQWR6CTM94WM04G0Z647", #source "../sources/Uncertainty-NIST-1900.lingua#r_75WCVW8CJG4TAFD3330T87588E", #metrology "../practice/Reference-life-cycle.lingua#r_1ZS7B98GYPWX6S7BFZ5S6CY6YR", #electromagnetism "../../../stem/physics/electromagnetism/measurement/From-fields-to-detector-signals-and-noise.lingua#r_3FQB4EV0F0QVWBSE9QBZDHT7AH", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../../../stem/physics/thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer/measurement/Infrared-temperatures-emissivity-reflections-and-size-of-source.lingua#r_31ERZY2WADAKFR6S1X10XFG43Y", #fluid-dynamics "../../../stem/physics/fluid-dynamics/measurement/Flow-visualization-PIV-and-uncertainty-in-derived-fields.lingua#r_1TH2QT61KGJF0Z9VGGY192G6VD") { r_5N7AJNW24YZV9CGHHEB0S6283T
**Read:** [Practical realizations of SI units — BIPM consultative committees](../sources/SI-Realizations.lingua#r_240WHEHDVW9TR241AXP6T4STM0), the applicable metre, candela/photometry, or nanometrology document; [Fundamental Good Practice in Dimensional Metrology — Flack and Hannaford](../sources/Dimensional-Metrology.lingua#r_5XRAV7WQWR6CTM94WM04G0Z647), optical-method discussions; [Simple Guide for Evaluating and Expressing Uncertainty — Possolo](../sources/Uncertainty-NIST-1900.lingua#r_75WCVW8CJG4TAFD3330T87588E), E26 Refractive Index.

Optical measurements require spectral, spatial, temporal, polarization, and geometric definitions where relevant. Radiant power, photometric output, illuminance, image intensity, wavelength, surface height, and a fitted film thickness are different quantities. A sensor’s counts become a result through a response and calibration model.

A simplified detector model can integrate spectral power times spectral responsivity and add background or dark response. Mismatch between the calibration spectrum and the specimen spectrum can matter even when total powers are equal. Photometric quantities add defined spectral weighting and geometry; an arbitrary camera brightness value is not an illuminance measurement.

Images also involve sampling, point-spread behavior, distortion, scale, noise, and an estimation algorithm. Pixel pitch or magnification alone does not establish the uncertainty of a detected boundary. In a thickness inferred from an optical model, refractive index, geometry, surface condition, and identifiability can dominate the result.

**Work:** compare a direct length image with an inverse optical estimate. Write the two measurement models, identify reference and algorithm versions, and show which information would distinguish scale error from boundary-definition ambiguity. Reconstruct TN 1900 E26 Refractive Index or a fully specified example from the dimensional sources, retaining correlations and model assumptions.

Read a complete relevant metre, photometry, or dimensional-nanometrology document for the advanced case. Then compare two independent techniques that interrogate related but not identical features. Agreement within appropriately defined uncertainty supports a bounded comparison; disagreement can reveal a measurand mismatch as well as a technical fault.

